1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,508
Meet Meeting Copilot, a private desktop assistant for live discussions.

2
00:00:04,708 --> 00:00:09,450
It helps you contribute useful questions and recommendations, while the meeting is still happening.

3
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:14,394
Choose your meeting playback device, and optionally include your microphone.

4
00:00:14,594 --> 00:00:19,227
Add a short brief, confirm participant consent, then start the live overlay.

5
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:25,284
When finalized speech reveals a useful gap, the overlay can suggest a grounded question.

6
00:00:25,484 --> 00:00:28,542
Open the explanation to review its evidence and uncertainty.

7
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:34,144
It can also propose an approach, not just ask another question.

8
00:00:34,344 --> 00:00:39,338
Here, a sample recommendation suggests backoff with jitter to spread retries during recovery.

9
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:44,279
Copy a suggestion, mark it already covered, or dismiss it.

10
00:00:44,479 --> 00:00:49,343
Browse earlier suggestions without posting anything to Teams. You decide what to say.

11
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:55,098
Analysis continues throughout longer meetings, with recent speech and relevant earlier context.

12
00:00:55,298 --> 00:00:59,450
Session history stays in memory until Stop, rather than waiting until the meeting ends.

13
00:01:00,450 --> 00:01:03,765
Keep Foundry, or select Gemini, Claude, or Grok.

14
00:01:03,965 --> 00:01:09,450
Each provider has its own encrypted credentials. Existing speech and teleprompter features stay independent.

15
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:14,284
Open AI compatible endpoints support cloud models and local servers.

16
00:01:14,484 --> 00:01:18,927
Test with synthetic text before a meeting. Azure Speech still handles audio.

17
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:23,903
For presentations, save your script in the built-in library.

18
00:01:24,103 --> 00:01:29,450
Open the reader without starting meeting capture. Your saved script stays separate from meeting context.

19
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:33,331
The minimal overlay keeps your script above your slides.

20
00:01:33,531 --> 00:01:39,450
Run starts offline timed scrolling. Stop holds your place. You can also scroll manually.

21
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:44,119
Voice following highlights matched words and holds position when you stop.

22
00:01:44,319 --> 00:01:49,377
Microphone audio goes to Azure Speech with your permission. Script matching stays local.

23
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:54,537
Capture exclusion depends on your sharing tool. Check another participant view.

24
00:01:54,737 --> 00:01:59,450
Review every suggestion. Meeting Copilot helps you contribute; you remain in control.
